1
00:00:07,426 --> 00:00:16,337
-==www.RagBear.com==-
是, 首相  第1季第6集

2
00:00:17,615 --> 00:00:25,384
<font color="#4096d1">本字幕仅供学习交流，严禁用于商业用途

3
00:00:25,384 --> 00:00:31,970
<font color="#4096d1">-=破烂熊字幕组=-
翻译: angel_liu
校对: tpring
时间轴: T-boy

4
00:00:35,741 --> 00:00:39,130
民主之胜

5
00:00:39,357 --> 00:00:42,950
昨夜酒会上 美国大使
I got some frightful pressure from the American ambassador

6
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:44,270
向我施加了可怕的压力
at that drinkies do last night.

7
00:00:44,517 --> 00:00:47,907
啊      他们听说我要取消三叉戟订单
Ah.        They'd heard about my cancelling Trident.

8
00:00:48,077 --> 00:00:49,669
啊
Ah.

9
00:00:49,837 --> 00:00:51,181
好像国防工业是
The American defence industries are

10
00:00:51,281 --> 00:00:53,899
美国总统政党的金库
big contributors to the President Party funds.

11
00:00:53,934 --> 00:00:58,707
啊      他说我们在东也门有大问题了
Ah.        He said we had a big problem in East Yemen.

12
00:00:58,877 --> 00:01:00,833
啊?
Ah?

13
00:01:01,037 --> 00:01:05,428
别这样"啊"来"啊"去的 伯纳 我又不是医生
Stop saying ''ah'' like that, Bernard. I'm not your doctor.

14
00:01:06,757 --> 00:01:09,635
对不起 首相      东也门的这个大问题是什么?
I'm sorry.        What is this big problem?

15
00:01:09,837 --> 00:01:11,793
啊...
Ah...

16
00:01:11,997 --> 00:01:14,989
谢谢 伯纳       我去想办法查
Thank you, Bernard.        I'll try to find out.

17
00:01:15,157 --> 00:01:18,239
他好像提了圣乔治岛
He muttered about St George's Island.

18
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:19,261
圣乔治岛?
St George's Island?

19
00:01:19,237 --> 00:01:22,856
是的 当真有个圣乔治岛?
Yes. There is a St George's Island,isn`t there?

20
00:01:22,956 --> 00:01:24,587
有 在英联邦
Yes, it's in the Commonwealth.

21
00:01:24,697 --> 00:01:27,595
啊 知道了 那个圣乔治岛
Ah, I see, yes. That St George's Island.

22
00:01:27,757 --> 00:01:32,130
他担心共产党想要夺取它
Apparently, he's afraid Communists might try to grab it.

23
00:01:32,030 --> 00:01:33,276
您怎么回答?
What did you say?

24
00:01:33,477 --> 00:01:35,829
我说我要咨询外交部      他怎么说?
I said I'd ask the Foreign Office.        What did he say?

25
00:01:35,929 --> 00:01:38,707
白宫认为外交部
The White House thinks the Foreign Office

26
00:01:38,708 --> 00:01:40,456
都是些左倾分子和卖国贼
is full of pinkos and traitors.

27
00:01:41,296 --> 00:01:43,009
不是的 呃 不全是
No, it's not. Well, not full.

28
00:01:43,717 --> 00:01:45,133
他们不想让红军取得
They don't want the Reds to get

29
00:01:45,233 --> 00:01:47,790
圣乔治岛这样的战略基地
a strategic base like St George's Island.

30
00:01:47,890 --> 00:01:51,524
他说要对英国对美出口征收关税
He spoke about putting tariffs on British exports to the USA

31
00:01:51,624 --> 00:01:53,472
对美国对英投资征税
and taxing US investment to Britain,

32
00:01:53,637 --> 00:01:55,787
以引起挤兑英镑的热潮
causing a run on the pound.

33
00:01:55,997 --> 00:01:57,926
您下午要会见外交部长 
Well, you are seeing the Foreign Secretary this afternoon. 

34
00:01:57,927 --> 00:01:58,996
不能让他解决吗?
Can't you get the Foreign Secretary to sort it out?

35
00:01:59,140 --> 00:02:01,118
毕竟他们在我们这边
After all, they are on our side.

36
00:02:01,317 --> 00:02:03,512
谁?      美国人
Who are?        The Americans.

37
00:02:03,717 --> 00:02:06,515
我还以为你说外交部
I thought you meant the Foreign Office.

38
00:02:07,517 --> 00:02:10,013
外交部在担心什么 迪克
What's the Foreign Office worried about then,  Dick?

39
00:02:10,113 --> 00:02:12,512
外交部长全听你的吧?
Have you got the Foreign Secretary eating out of your hand.

40
00:02:12,677 --> 00:02:14,401
没错 管教得非常好
Oh, yes. Completely house-trained.

41
00:02:14,402 --> 00:02:15,872
那还有什么问题?
 So what is the problem?

42
00:02:16,237 --> 00:02:17,971
问题是首相
The Prime Minister's the problem.

43
00:02:18,071 --> 00:02:21,949
他开始不相信外交部长的意见了
He's starting to mistrust our advice.

44
00:02:22,157 --> 00:02:26,992
他甚至质疑外交部的政策      不会吧
He even questioned Foreign Office policy.        Surely not!

45
00:02:27,197 --> 00:02:28,173
我们甚至感觉到内阁
We even see a danger the Cabinet

46
00:02:28,273 --> 00:02:30,827
自行制定外交政策的危险
may pursue its own foreign policy.

47
00:02:31,037 --> 00:02:31,582
但那太荒谬了
But that's absurd.

48
00:02:31,682 --> 00:02:35,156
一个国家不能有两个外交政策
The country can't have two foreign policies

49
00:02:35,357 --> 00:02:36,832
没错 而且首相
Quite. And the PM's getting

50
00:02:36,932 --> 00:02:39,874
太急于讨好白宫了
far too keen on keeping the White House happy.

51
00:02:40,077 --> 00:02:42,671
天哪天哪 有什么要帮忙的?
Dear, oh, dear. So, how can I help?

52
00:02:42,877 --> 00:02:44,159
现在发生了些事
There are a couple of things coming up

53
00:02:44,259 --> 00:02:47,668
需要指导他一下
where he might need guiding in the right direction.

54
00:02:47,837 --> 00:02:51,830
其中一个是圣乔治岛      啊 对对对
One is St George's Island.        Ah. Oh, yes, yes, yes.

55
00:02:51,997 --> 00:02:54,955
能提醒我一下吗? 迪克
Remind me, would you, Dick?

56
00:02:55,157 --> 00:02:59,333
如你所知 这是位于印度洋的少数几个
As you know, it's one of the few islands in the Indian Ocean

57
00:02:59,433 --> 00:03:01,757
独立后仍属于英联邦的岛屿之一
to stay in the Commonwealth after the Independence.

58
00:03:01,957 --> 00:03:04,915
啊 对 没错 很民主 是吧?
Oh, yes, that's right. It's quite democratic.

59
00:03:05,117 --> 00:03:06,741
是的 自由选举之类的
Yes. Free elections and everything.

60
00:03:06,776 --> 00:03:10,521
但山林中有群左翼游击队
But there's a group of Marxist guerrillas in the mountains.

61
00:03:10,556 --> 00:03:13,389
我们收到情报 他们预谋发动政变
We are getting reports that they're planning a coup.

62
00:03:13,597 --> 00:03:15,042
这些事总会发生的
Well, these things will happen.

63
00:03:16,557 --> 00:03:19,143
他们并不打算自己发起
They're not thinking of starting it on their own.

64
00:03:19,243 --> 00:03:20,949
东也门会提供援助
East Yemen is helping.

65
00:03:21,157 --> 00:03:22,255
东也门不是民主国家吗?
Isn't that a democracy?

66
00:03:22,355 --> 00:03:26,551
全称是东也门人民民主共和国
People's Democratic Republic of East Yemen.

67
00:03:26,757 --> 00:03:29,351
知道了 左翼独裁政权
Oh, I see. It's a Communist dictatorship.

68
00:03:29,517 --> 00:03:32,509
那些游击队是由苏维埃援助的吗?
And the guerrillas are Soviet-backed, aren`t they?

69
00:03:32,717 --> 00:03:34,676
是 利比亚也在背后支援
Yes, and Libyan-backed.

70
00:03:34,776 --> 00:03:37,951
所以外交部明显打算置身事外
Obviously, we in the Foreign Office are staying right out of it.

71
00:03:38,157 --> 00:03:40,034
是的 很明显
Obviously.

72
00:03:40,237 --> 00:03:43,991
我们参与 也只会扰乱几个非洲锋线国家而已
It would only upset a load of frontline African states.

73
00:03:44,197 --> 00:03:46,836
而我们现在还不想对抗苏维埃
And we don't want to antagonise the Soviets.

74
00:03:47,037 --> 00:03:50,267
正是 而且我们刚签了份大合约
Quite. And we've just landed a huge contract

75
00:03:50,367 --> 00:03:52,829
要在圣乔治岛建设机场和港口
to build a new St George's airport and harbour.

76
00:03:52,997 --> 00:03:55,750
一旦站错立场 就会失去这份合约
If we back the wrong side, we may lose it.

77
00:03:55,957 --> 00:03:59,433
我们不介意哪边赢 民主政党还是马克思主义者?
We don't mind which side wins,the democrats or the Marxists?

78
00:04:00,717 --> 00:04:03,106
为何要介意呢? 但还是有问题
Why should we? But you see the problem.

79
00:04:03,277 --> 00:04:07,333
如果首相的丘吉尔式爱国心大爆发
If the PM gets into one of his ghastly patriotic Churchillian moods,

80
00:04:07,433 --> 00:04:08,068
他会干预的
he may intervene.

81
00:04:08,237 --> 00:04:11,627
那些向英国看齐 捍卫民主的废话
All that pro-British, defending democracy nonsense.

82
00:04:11,837 --> 00:04:14,749
我知道 我知道
Oh, I know, I know.

83
00:04:14,957 --> 00:04:16,608
他必须了解一旦你着手
He must understand that once you start

84
00:04:16,708 --> 00:04:19,952
干预别国内部争端
interfering in the internal squabbles of other countries,

85
00:04:20,117 --> 00:04:22,032
你就岌岌可危了
you're on a very slippery slope.

86
00:04:22,132 --> 00:04:24,748
连外交部长都明白
Even the Foreign Secretary's grasped that.

87
00:04:25,797 --> 00:04:28,834
另一个问题是什么?
Really? So what was the other point?

88
00:04:29,037 --> 00:04:30,864
阿拉伯已经提出议案
The Arabs have put down a motion

89
00:04:30,964 --> 00:04:33,336
要联合国谴责以色列
at the United Nations condemning Israel.

90
00:04:33,397 --> 00:04:36,389
我们当然投票支持阿拉伯      当然
Naturally, we'll vote on the Arab side.        Naturally.

91
00:04:36,557 --> 00:04:39,142
但我想首相要我们弃权
But I gather the PM wants us to abstain.

92
00:04:39,242 --> 00:04:40,790
怎么可以! 为什么?
Surely not! Why?

93
00:04:40,997 --> 00:04:42,704
说这次是巴解组织挑事
Something about the PLO starting it this time,

94
00:04:42,804 --> 00:04:46,789
双方都有错 感情用事
faults on both sides. Sentimental nonsense.

95
00:04:46,957 --> 00:04:49,391
拍美国马屁 一如往常
Sucking up to the Americans, as always.

96
00:04:49,597 --> 00:04:51,825
只需让他知道
Just help him to realise that,

97
00:04:51,925 --> 00:04:54,388
牵涉到外交事务时
as far as foreign affairs are concerned,

98
00:04:54,557 --> 00:04:57,890
他的工作仅限于公关接待
his job is to confine himself to the hospitality

99
00:04:57,990 --> 00:04:59,678
热情好客
and ceremonial role.

100
00:04:59,877 --> 00:05:00,527
我尽力
I'll do my best,

101
00:05:00,627 --> 00:05:03,268
但你知道政客进入10号会怎样
but you know what happens when politicians get into Number 10.

102
00:05:03,944 --> 00:05:06,120
他们想在世界舞台上占个位置
They want their place on the world stage.

103
00:05:07,161 --> 00:05:09,021
站在舞台上的是演员
People on stages are called actors.

104
00:05:09,097 --> 00:05:11,504
他们只需作稳健状
All they're required to do is look plausible,

105
00:05:11,604 --> 00:05:14,374
保持清醒 按部就班念台词
stay sober and say the lines they're given in the right order

106
00:05:16,117 --> 00:05:18,756
一些人试图自己想词
Some of them try to make up their own lines

107
00:05:18,957 --> 00:05:21,596
立刻就下台了
They don't last long.

108
00:05:24,837 --> 00:05:27,749
昨晚美国大使和我私下谈了谈
The American ambassador had a word with me last night.

109
00:05:27,917 --> 00:05:30,954
关于什么?      你对圣乔治岛了解多少?
About what?       What do you know about St George's Island?

110
00:05:37,357 --> 00:05:39,666
您对它了解多少?
What do you know about it?

111
00:05:39,877 --> 00:05:42,471
外交部长是你 不是我
Well, you're the Foreign Secretary, not me!

112
00:05:44,157 --> 00:05:46,546
有左翼接管的危险吗?
Is there any danger of a Communist takeover?

113
00:05:46,757 --> 00:05:49,749
呃 他说有吗?      他暗示有
Well, did he say there was?        He hinted.

114
00:05:50,917 --> 00:05:53,462
不 绝不可能
No. No chance at all. No chance at all.

115
00:05:53,562 --> 00:05:56,072
不然外交部会告诉我的
The Foreign Office would have told me.

116
00:05:56,277 --> 00:05:58,627
你肯定他们什么都告诉你?
You're sure they always tell you everything?

117
00:05:58,727 --> 00:06:01,989
只要他们认为我该知道的
Well, everything they think I should know.

118
00:06:02,197 --> 00:06:03,144
我就怕这个
That's what I'm afraid of.

119
00:06:03,244 --> 00:06:05,161
美国人很担心 
The Americans are worried 

120
00:06:05,162 --> 00:06:07,609
我们现在不能惹他们
and we can't afford to upset them at the moment.

121
00:06:07,797 --> 00:06:09,535
我们肯定已经控制了事态
I'm sure we've got everything under control.

122
00:06:09,635 --> 00:06:13,031
张伯伦还以为控制了希特勒呢
Chamberlain thought Hitler was under control.

123
00:06:13,237 --> 00:06:14,732
张伯伦
Ah, well, Chamberlain.

124
00:06:14,832 --> 00:06:17,151
艾登还以为控制了纳塞尔呢
Eden thought Nasser was under control.

125
00:06:17,357 --> 00:06:19,158
外交部不知道自己在做什么?
The F.O. doesn't know what it's doing?

126
00:06:19,258 --> 00:06:22,148
不 他们不交待他们在做什么
No, they don't tell us what they're doing!

127
00:06:23,237 --> 00:06:26,991
可笑 他们详细回答我提出的每个问题
Absurd. They give me a full answer to any questions I ask.

128
00:06:27,197 --> 00:06:29,995
你没问的呢?      例如?
And the ones you don't ask?        Such as?

129
00:06:30,157 --> 00:06:31,313
例如圣乔治岛
Such as about St George's Island.

130
00:06:31,413 --> 00:06:34,993
我不问这些问题
Ah, well, I don't ask those.

131
00:06:35,197 --> 00:06:36,703
问问他们 帮我个忙 行吗?
Well, just ask them. For me. All right?

132
00:06:36,803 --> 00:06:38,567
当然 您非要问的话
Yes, of course. If that is what you want

133
00:06:38,945 --> 00:06:39,817
但别忘了 
But don`t foget.

134
00:06:39,818 --> 00:06:43,250
一旦您干预别国内部争端
Once you interfere in other countries' internal squabbles,

135
00:06:43,326 --> 00:06:44,862
您就岌岌可危了
you're on a very slippery slope.

136
00:06:46,210 --> 00:06:46,994
还有什么?
Anything else?

137
00:06:47,397 --> 00:06:49,446
有 据说我们今晚要在联合国投票
Yes, I gather we're proposing to vote against

138
00:06:49,546 --> 00:06:52,472
反对以色列 为什么?
Israel in the UN tonight. Why?

139
00:06:52,677 --> 00:06:54,709
他们炸了巴解组织
They bombed the PLO.

140
00:06:54,809 --> 00:06:55,987
巴解组织也炸了以色列
The PLO bombed Israel.

141
00:06:55,999 --> 00:06:58,376
但以色列炸弹扔得比较多
But the Israelis dropped more bombs than the PLO!

142
00:06:58,431 --> 00:06:59,834
巴解组织挑头
The PLO started it!

143
00:07:00,037 --> 00:07:01,007
不 他们没有
No, they didn't.

144
00:07:01,516 --> 00:07:04,475
我看双方都有错
It seems to me there are faults on both sides.

145
00:07:04,677 --> 00:07:05,821
我的消息不是这样的
Not according to my advice.

146
00:07:05,919 --> 00:07:09,075
美国很忧虑 想要我们弃权
America is worried. They want us to abstain.

147
00:07:09,797 --> 00:07:11,103
我觉得我们不能
I don't think we could do that.

148
00:07:11,203 --> 00:07:13,996
怎么?      外交部不会同意的
Why not?        The Foreign Office wouldn't wear it.

149
00:07:14,197 --> 00:07:16,230
是他们听我们的
Are they here to follow our instructions or

150
00:07:16,330 --> 00:07:17,986
还是我们听他们的?
are we to follow theirs?

151
00:07:18,197 --> 00:07:20,347
别傻了
Now, don't be silly.

152
00:07:23,957 --> 00:07:26,346
首相 汉弗莱爵士到了
Prime Minister, Sir Humphrey's here.

153
00:07:26,517 --> 00:07:29,111
首相      汉弗莱 我很担心
Prime Minister.        Humphrey, I'm worried.

154
00:07:29,277 --> 00:07:31,666
什么事 首相?
Oh, what about, Prime Minister?

155
00:07:33,357 --> 00:07:34,381
美国人
About the Americans.

156
00:07:34,481 --> 00:07:38,193
对 我们都担心美国人
Well, we're all worried about the Americans.

157
00:07:38,397 --> 00:07:40,135
外交是门复杂营生 对吗?
Foreign affairs are a complicated business,aren`t they?

158
00:07:40,235 --> 00:07:43,995
没错 首相 所以扔给外交部处理
Yes,That's why we leave it to the Foreign Office.

159
00:07:44,197 --> 00:07:46,593
将来几个月我得跟美国搞好关系 
I've got to keep in with the Americans for the next few months 

160
00:07:46,594 --> 00:07:48,368
为取消大额国防订单打基础
if I'm to cancel our defence order.

161
00:07:48,403 --> 00:07:53,157
昨晚我猜他们也很担心我们
Ah. I gather that they're worried about us.

162
00:07:53,257 --> 00:07:57,512
他们当然担心 不过我知道怎样与他们搞好关系
Of course they are, but I know how to keep in with them.

163
00:07:57,717 --> 00:08:00,629
怎样?       别取消大额国防订单
How?        Don't cancel the huge defence order.

164
00:08:00,837 --> 00:08:02,541
不 汉弗莱 我决定了
No, Humphrey, I'm determined on that,

165
00:08:02,641 --> 00:08:04,701
但别的方面不能再惹他们
but we mustn't upset them in any other way.

166
00:08:04,801 --> 00:08:08,611
大使提到了圣乔治岛
The ambassador mentioned St George's Island.

167
00:08:09,797 --> 00:08:13,928
噢 真的?      世界那头出什么事了?
Oh, really?       What's going on in that part of the world?

168
00:08:15,077 --> 00:08:16,697
世界哪头?
What part of the world?

169
00:08:17,677 --> 00:08:20,923
那头 圣乔治岛那头
That part. The part where St George's Island is.

170
00:08:22,517 --> 00:08:23,641
那是哪头?
What part is that?

171
00:08:24,917 --> 00:08:27,431
如果你不知道 汉弗莱 建议你看看地图
I suggest you go and have a look at the map!

172
00:08:27,531 --> 00:08:29,031
不 我知道 首相
No, I do know, Prime Minister.

173
00:08:29,131 --> 00:08:31,078
好 那我们都知道了
Good. Then we both know.

174
00:08:34,757 --> 00:08:39,433
白宫担心它会被马克思主义者接管
The White House is worried it might be taken over by Marxists.

175
00:08:40,757 --> 00:08:41,637
这不好笑 汉弗莱
It's not funny, Humphrey.

176
00:08:41,737 --> 00:08:43,847
对 不好笑 很感人 真的
No, indeed. Rather touching, really.

177
00:08:44,917 --> 00:08:47,782
首相 一旦您开始干预
Prime Minister, once you start interfering

178
00:08:47,882 --> 00:08:49,912
别国内部争端
in the internal squabbles of other countries,

179
00:08:50,077 --> 00:08:51,543
您就岌岌可危了
you're on a very slippery slope.

180
00:08:52,837 --> 00:08:54,652
外交部长刚这么说过
That's what the Foreign Secretary said.

181
00:08:55,387 --> 00:08:56,700
真奇怪
Extraordinary.

182
00:08:57,397 --> 00:09:00,397
还有今晚联合国对以色列的投票
Then there's the U.N. vote on Israel tonight.

183
00:09:00,497 --> 00:09:02,442
美国要我们弃权
The Americans want us to abstain.

184
00:09:02,717 --> 00:09:06,986
这是对阿拉伯关系问题
It's a question of maintaining our relationship with the Arabs.

185
00:09:07,202 --> 00:09:08,409
伊斯兰政权
The power of Islam.

186
00:09:09,093 --> 00:09:10,498
石油供应
Oil supplies.

187
00:09:10,957 --> 00:09:13,312
汉弗莱 我在说是非问题
I'm talking about what's right and wrong.

188
00:09:13,517 --> 00:09:16,077
可别让外交部听到
Well, don't let the Foreign Office hear you.

189
00:09:16,237 --> 00:09:18,896
如果您非要不偏不倚
If you insist on an even-handed approach,

190
00:09:18,991 --> 00:09:22,149
外交部可能同意弃权
the Foreign Office might agree to abstaining,

191
00:09:22,184 --> 00:09:24,145
只要您授权我们在那的人
so long as you authorise our man there

192
00:09:24,245 --> 00:09:26,512
公开发言抨击犹太复国主义
to make a powerful speech attacking Zionism.

193
00:09:26,997 --> 00:09:30,273
我们当然要发扬和平 和谐 善意吧
Surely we should promote peace, harmony, goodwill.

194
00:09:30,477 --> 00:09:32,866
那就很奇怪了
Well, it would be most unusual.

195
00:09:33,037 --> 00:09:34,869
联合国是公认的
The U.N. is the accepted forum

196
00:09:34,969 --> 00:09:36,830
表达国际憎恶的平台
for the expression of international hatred.

197
00:09:37,637 --> 00:09:39,219
捍卫圣乔治岛的民主呢?
And defending democracy on St George's?

198
00:09:39,319 --> 00:09:43,569
如果会伤害友邦 殃及英国利益 那就免了
Not if it harms us by upsetting our friends.

199
00:09:43,797 --> 00:09:46,834
汉弗莱 难道英国不该支持法律和正义?
Britain should not support law and justice?

200
00:09:47,037 --> 00:09:48,456
当然应该 首相
Of course we should. Prime Minister.

201
00:09:48,914 --> 00:09:52,016
只要不影响外交政策就行
We just shouldn't let it affect our foreign policy, that's all.

202
00:09:53,077 --> 00:09:55,466
我们应该锄强扶弱
We must fight for the weak against the strong.

203
00:09:55,677 --> 00:09:58,798
那派军队去阿富汗对抗俄国啊
Then send troops to Afghanistan to fight the Russians.

204
00:10:00,478 --> 00:10:01,628
俄国强过头了
The Russians are too strong.

205
00:10:04,957 --> 00:10:07,346
那法律和正义呢?
What was that about law and justice?

206
00:10:07,557 --> 00:10:11,948
尽管如此 汉弗莱 我想要向圣乔治岛民选首相保证
I want assurances sent to the Prime Minister of St George's Island

207
00:10:12,117 --> 00:10:14,426
英国会支持他的
that Britain will stand by him.

208
00:10:14,637 --> 00:10:17,239
与外交部长讨论吧
Discuss this with the Foreign Secretary.

209
00:10:17,339 --> 00:10:18,840
谢谢 汉弗莱
Thank you, Humphrey.

210
00:10:19,197 --> 00:10:23,588
谢谢 首相       你真帮了大忙
Thank you, Prime Minister.        You've been a great help

211
00:10:24,757 --> 00:10:27,351
伯纳?      在 首相
Bernard?        Yes, Prime Minister?

212
00:10:27,517 --> 00:10:29,712
圣乔治岛到底在哪?
Where exactly is St George's Island?

213
00:10:32,717 --> 00:10:34,586
看看地球仪吧?
Shall we look at the globe?

214
00:10:34,686 --> 00:10:37,057
私人办公室有一个      好主意
There is one in the private office.        Good idea.

215
00:10:41,957 --> 00:10:45,950
下午好 路克      下午好 首相
Good afternoon, Luke.        Good afternoon, Prime Minister.

216
00:10:46,117 --> 00:10:48,312
在哪呢?
Now, where is it?

217
00:10:52,317 --> 00:10:56,310
在这儿 阿拉伯海      接近波斯湾
It's here, in the Arabian Sea.        Near the Persian Gulf.

218
00:10:56,477 --> 00:10:57,450
西方的生命线
The lifeline of the West.

219
00:10:57,550 --> 00:11:00,368
这是阿富汗 由苏维埃控制
There's Afghanistan, now under Soviet control.

220
00:11:01,237 --> 00:11:03,626
阿拉伯海以北400英里
Only 400 miles north of the Arabian Sea.

221
00:11:03,797 --> 00:11:07,154
如果苏维埃夺取巴基斯坦... 他们不会的
If the Soviets ever took Pakistan...Which they wouldn't.

222
00:11:07,957 --> 00:11:10,779
如果会 他们就控制了波斯湾
If they did, they'd control the Persian Gulf,

223
00:11:10,879 --> 00:11:12,745
阿拉伯海 印度洋
the Arabian Sea and the Indian Ocean.

224
00:11:13,117 --> 00:11:16,712
他们一直都想要个"温水港"
They've always wanted a ''warm water port''.

225
00:11:16,917 --> 00:11:18,969
他们不会入侵巴基斯坦
They wouldn't invade Pakistan.

226
00:11:19,069 --> 00:11:21,882
美国有舰队永久驻扎
The Americans have a fleet permanently stationed here.

227
00:11:22,077 --> 00:11:24,671
印度洋
The Indian Ocean.

228
00:11:25,957 --> 00:11:30,348
首相 能和您说说...国内事务吗?
Prime Minister, may I have a word about...home affairs?

229
00:11:30,517 --> 00:11:33,429
国内事务?      是的
Home affairs?        Yes.

230
00:11:33,637 --> 00:11:35,463
不能等等吗? 我们在讨论外交事务
Can`t you wait? We're discussing foreign affairs.

231
00:11:35,563 --> 00:11:37,741
不 首相 事情紧急
No, Prime Minister, it's rather urgent.

232
00:11:39,357 --> 00:11:40,957
你没事吧 伯纳?
Are you all right, Bernard?

233
00:11:41,057 --> 00:11:42,412
没事 首相 求您
Yes, Prime Minister. Please.

234
00:11:43,317 --> 00:11:45,706
好吧 失陪 路克
Very well. Excuse me, Luke.

235
00:11:48,757 --> 00:11:50,433
到底什么事?
What on earth's the matter?

236
00:11:50,533 --> 00:11:52,100
我不想不忠诚
I don't want to be disloyal,

237
00:11:52,517 --> 00:11:54,772
但当着路克的面
but it wasn't a good idea to continue that conversation

238
00:11:54,872 --> 00:11:57,530
谈这些不好 安全问题
in front of Luke. Security.

239
00:11:57,717 --> 00:12:00,256
他是你的同事 我的私人秘书之一
He's your colleague, one of my private secretaries.

240
00:12:00,356 --> 00:12:02,334
军情六处干什么吃的?
What is MI6 up to...?

241
00:12:03,237 --> 00:12:06,108
不是那种问题 他为外交部工作
Not that sort of risk. He works for the F.O.

242
00:12:06,208 --> 00:12:07,138
他为我工作
He works for me.

243
00:12:07,637 --> 00:12:12,836
没错 但他不仅是外交部派给你的人
Eh.yes, but he's not only your man from the Foreign Office,

244
00:12:12,997 --> 00:12:14,876
他也是10号里他们的人
he's also their man in Number 10.

245
00:12:15,849 --> 00:12:17,209
安插进来的
He's a plant.

246
00:12:21,877 --> 00:12:25,074
您明白吗?      明白 不明白
Do you understand?        Yes. No!

247
00:12:26,877 --> 00:12:31,075
你是说外交部有事瞒我?      是的
The F.O. is keeping something from me?        Yes.

248
00:12:31,237 --> 00:12:35,594
什么事?      不知道 他们也没告诉我
What?        I don't know. They're keeping it from me, too.

249
00:12:35,797 --> 00:12:36,954
那你又怎么知道的?      我不知道
Then how do you know?        I don't know.

250
00:12:37,436 --> 00:12:39,642
你刚说外交部有事瞒我
You just said the F.O. was keeping something from me.

251
00:12:39,643 --> 00:12:41,006
若你不知道 你又怎么知道?
How do you know if you don't know?

252
00:12:41,917 --> 00:12:43,913
我不知道具体是什么
I don't know specifically what,

253
00:12:43,914 --> 00:12:47,062
但我知道他们对所有人瞒着所有事
but I do know they always keep everything from everybody.

254
00:12:47,077 --> 00:12:49,637
是惯例      那谁知道?
It's normal practice.        Who does know?

255
00:12:49,837 --> 00:12:52,226
我来理清问题好吗?
May I just clarify the question?

256
00:12:52,397 --> 00:12:54,135
您问谁知道那些我不知道
You are asking who would know what it is that I don't know

257
00:12:54,235 --> 00:12:56,656
您也不知道 但外交部知道
and you don't know but the F.O. know that they know

258
00:12:56,881 --> 00:12:58,479
他们不让您知道 
that they are keeping from you 

259
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:00,341
所以您不知道
so you don't know and they do know

260
00:13:00,376 --> 00:13:01,601
我们只知道他们瞒着我们 
all we know is there is something we don't know 

261
00:13:01,602 --> 00:13:02,377
而我们需要知道
and we want to know,

262
00:13:02,423 --> 00:13:07,884
但我们不知道是什么的事 对吗?
but we don't know what because we don't know? Is that it?

263
00:13:08,357 --> 00:13:10,633
我来理清吧
May I clarify the question?

264
00:13:11,237 --> 00:13:13,989
除了外交部 还有谁知道外交部的秘密?
Who knows Foreign Office secrets apart from the Foreign Office?

265
00:13:14,031 --> 00:13:16,951
这简单 只有俄国
Oh, that's easy. Only the Kremlin.

266
00:13:20,157 --> 00:13:23,866
圣乔治岛的事真令人厌烦
This bother about St George's Island is getting to be a bore.

267
00:13:24,077 --> 00:13:27,911
20年前我们让他们独立 就是一大错误
We made the real mistake giving them their independence.

268
00:13:28,117 --> 00:13:30,711
大势所趋吧 变革的洪流之类?
Wasn't that right? Wind of change and all?

269
00:13:30,877 --> 00:13:34,870
对 不过方式错了 当初应该分割那个岛
Yes, but not that way. We should have partitioned the island.

270
00:13:35,037 --> 00:13:38,916
就像我们分割印度 塞浦路斯 巴勒斯坦 爱尔兰?
Like we did in India, Cyprus and Palestine? And Ireland?

271
00:13:39,041 --> 00:13:42,834
没错 那是我们一贯的殖民地独立政策
Yes, that was our invariable practice with the colonies.

272
00:13:42,934 --> 00:13:44,034
从未失效
It always worked.

273
00:13:45,357 --> 00:13:47,746
分割国家不是总引起内战吗?
But didn't partition always lead to civil war?

274
00:13:47,917 --> 00:13:50,698
像印度 塞浦路斯 巴勒斯坦和爱尔兰那样
As in India, Cyprus, Palestine and Ireland.

275
00:13:51,452 --> 00:13:52,987
没错 但也使他们有事可做
Yes, but it kept them busy.

276
00:13:53,077 --> 00:13:57,593
不与其他国家打仗 自己同自己打
Instead of fighting other people, they fought each other.

277
00:13:57,797 --> 00:14:02,075
对 挺好的 省得我们定政策 干杯
Yes, rather good. Saved us having a policy. Cheers.

278
00:14:03,077 --> 00:14:05,875
汉弗莱爵士      嗯 伯纳?
Sir Humphrey?        Yes, Bernard?

279
00:14:06,037 --> 00:14:08,835
汉弗莱爵士      嗯 伯纳?
Um, Sir Humphrey...        Yes, Bernard?

280
00:14:08,997 --> 00:14:11,386
能谈谈吗?      好的 伯纳
Could I have a word?        Yes, Bernard?

281
00:14:11,557 --> 00:14:13,946
和你们俩      好 什么事?
With both of you.        Yes. What about?

282
00:14:14,117 --> 00:14:16,108
圣乔治岛      又怎么了?
St George's.        What now?

283
00:14:16,317 --> 00:14:19,070
貌似首相完全不了解情况
The PM seems to be completely in the dark.

284
00:14:19,277 --> 00:14:23,714
好      非常好 还有什么?
Good.        Excellent. Anything else?

285
00:14:23,917 --> 00:14:26,590
我在想 是不是有什么事他不知道?
I wonder, is there anything he doesn't know?

286
00:14:26,797 --> 00:14:29,186
我都不知从哪说起 伯纳
I hardly know where to begin, Bernard.

287
00:14:31,077 --> 00:14:33,351
不 我是说重要的事
No, I mean anything important.

288
00:14:33,352 --> 00:14:35,262
外交部长会告诉他的
He has the Foreign Secretary to tell him.

289
00:14:35,797 --> 00:14:38,727
他好像觉得外交部长也不全知道
He seems to think he doesn't know either.

290
00:14:38,728 --> 00:14:39,922
那可不是
I should hope not!

291
00:14:41,357 --> 00:14:44,566
你是在暗示首相应该知道吗?
Are you implying that he ought to know what is happening?

292
00:14:44,567 --> 00:14:46,514
他是首相啊
Well, he is the Prime Minister.

293
00:14:46,717 --> 00:14:49,675
对 可是伯纳 让政客
Bernard, it's simply too dangerous to let politicians

294
00:14:49,710 --> 00:14:51,508
参与外交太危险了
become involved with diplomacy.

295
00:14:51,613 --> 00:14:54,392
外交旨在存活到下世纪
Diplomacy is about surviving until the next century.

296
00:14:54,759 --> 00:14:57,533
政治旨在存活到星期五下午
Politics is about surviving to the Friday afternoon!

297
00:14:59,428 --> 00:15:01,490
世界上有157个独立国家
There are 157 independent countries in the world.

298
00:15:01,491 --> 00:15:03,041
我们和他们打了多年交道了
We've dealt with them for years.

299
00:15:03,117 --> 00:15:06,029
几乎全体议员都对此一窍不通
There's hardly an MP who knows anything.

300
00:15:06,197 --> 00:15:07,823
给他们张世界地图
Show them a map of the world,

301
00:15:07,824 --> 00:15:10,078
大多数人连怀特岛都找不到(英国南部)
most have a job finding the Isle of Wight.

302
00:15:11,237 --> 00:15:13,360
政客不会这么无知吧?
Surely politicians can't be that ignorant?

303
00:15:15,357 --> 00:15:16,957
非常好 坐下 伯纳
Very well. Sit down, Bernard.

304
00:15:17,917 --> 00:15:20,909
上伏塔在哪?(西非伏塔河上游)      嗯
Where is the Upper Volta?       Em...

305
00:15:21,077 --> 00:15:24,069
乍得的首都叫什么?      嗯
What's the capital of Chad?        Um...

306
00:15:24,237 --> 00:15:28,708
马里的官方语言是什么?      嗯
What language do they speak in Mali?        Em...

307
00:15:28,917 --> 00:15:32,626
秘鲁的总统是谁?      嗯
Who's the president of Peru?       Um...

308
00:15:32,837 --> 00:15:35,431
喀麦隆信奉什么国教?
What is the national religion of Cameroon?

309
00:15:36,637 --> 00:15:38,977
嗯      伯纳?
Em...        Bernard?

310
00:15:39,877 --> 00:15:42,266
你应该参选议员
You should stand for Parliament.

311
00:15:43,677 --> 00:15:46,000
不 我是说在我们民主国家
No, what I mean is if it's a democracy,

312
00:15:46,001 --> 00:15:48,220
大家难道不讨论吗?
shouldn't people sort of discuss things a bit?

313
00:15:48,797 --> 00:15:51,709
当然 充分讨论       不参考事实吗?
Of course. Full discussion.        And have the facts?

314
00:15:51,917 --> 00:15:53,099
当然不!
Of course not!

315
00:15:53,100 --> 00:15:56,299
他们不需要 事实只会把问题搞复杂
They don't want them. Facts complicate things.

316
00:15:56,334 --> 00:15:58,665
媒体 人民和他们选的领袖
All the press, the people and their elected leaders

317
00:15:58,666 --> 00:16:01,217
只想知道谁好谁坏
want to know is who are the goodies and baddies.

318
00:16:02,077 --> 00:16:04,802
问题是为了国家利益
The interests of Britain nearly always involve doing

319
00:16:04,803 --> 00:16:07,192
总得和人们认为的坏人做交易
deals with people they think are baddies.

320
00:16:07,557 --> 00:16:10,435
以及偶尔抛弃不合作的好人
And not helping the goodies occasionally.

321
00:16:10,637 --> 00:16:13,231
所以我们避免讨论外交事务
So we avoid discussion of foreign affairs.

322
00:16:13,397 --> 00:16:15,786
或者只在外交部之内讨论
Or rather we keep it inside the Foreign Office

323
00:16:15,957 --> 00:16:18,369
只制定一项政策 提交外交部长
then we produce one policy for the Foreign Secretary,

324
00:16:18,370 --> 00:16:20,162
那就是我们的结论
which is our considered view.

325
00:16:20,825 --> 00:16:22,169
他照办
And he can act upon it.

326
00:16:22,204 --> 00:16:25,312
没有其他选择?没有备选方案?      没有
No options? No alternatives?        None.

327
00:16:25,517 --> 00:16:26,766
如果他不满意呢?
What if he's not satisfied?

328
00:16:26,767 --> 00:16:29,530
要是他敦促 我们会再看看
If pressed, we look at it again.

329
00:16:29,997 --> 00:16:30,844
并得出另一结论?
And come up with a different view?

330
00:16:30,845 --> 00:16:33,155
当然不是 同一结论
Of course not! We come up with the same view.

331
00:16:34,397 --> 00:16:37,389
要是他非要选择呢?      显然 伯纳
What if he demands options?        It's obvious.

332
00:16:37,557 --> 00:16:39,915
外交部会给他三个选择
The F.O. present him with three options,

333
00:16:39,916 --> 00:16:43,146
其中两个实际上完全一样
two of which are, in fact, exactly the same.

334
00:16:43,637 --> 00:16:45,832
第三个则完全不能接受
And the third is totally unacceptable.

335
00:16:46,037 --> 00:16:48,710
比如轰炸华沙或入侵法国
Like bombing Warsaw or invading France.

336
00:16:48,917 --> 00:16:51,898
有时我们鼓励外交部长
We occasionally encourage the Foreign Secretary to

337
00:16:51,899 --> 00:16:53,965
自己出政策
produce his own policy,

338
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:57,362
然后告诉他不出48小时
then we tell him it will inevitably lead to World War Three,

339
00:16:57,363 --> 00:16:59,480
那必将引发第三次世界大战
perhaps within 48 hours.

340
00:16:59,837 --> 00:17:02,832
知道了 我真笨 对不起
I see. I'm sorry to appear stupid...

341
00:17:02,833 --> 00:17:05,094
说哪里话 伯纳
Oh, perish the thought, Bernard.

342
00:17:06,757 --> 00:17:09,285
可据我经验 大臣很在乎
In my experience, ministers are concerned about

343
00:17:09,286 --> 00:17:12,100
政策对国内政治意见的影响
the effect of policy on domestic opinion.

344
00:17:12,117 --> 00:17:14,506
这个体系似乎不允许这样
Our system doesn't seem to allow for that.

345
00:17:14,717 --> 00:17:16,751
当然不 我们关注全球
Of course not. We take the global view.

346
00:17:16,752 --> 00:17:19,061
以世界利益为准
We ask what's best for the world.

347
00:17:19,637 --> 00:17:23,346
多数大臣关心<每日邮报>会怎么说
Most ministers would ask what will the ''Daily Mail'' say!

348
00:17:23,557 --> 00:17:27,312
伯纳 我们不能把外交政策
We can't have foreign policy made by yobbos

349
00:17:27,313 --> 00:17:30,256
交给报界编辑或后座议员这类流氓
like Fleet Street editors or backbench MPs!

350
00:17:30,291 --> 00:17:32,909
或内阁大臣      或内阁大臣
Or Cabinet ministers.        Or Cabinet ministers.

351
00:17:33,077 --> 00:17:34,859
我们作正确决定
We take the right decisions

352
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:37,191
让他们解决政治问题
and let them sort out the politics later.

353
00:17:37,237 --> 00:17:42,759
谁? 好的 请进 惠特莫夫人 谢谢
Yes? Yes, come in, Mrs Whitmore. Thank you.

354
00:17:42,894 --> 00:17:46,596
如果外交部长不接受外交部的意见...?
If the Foreign Secretary won't accept this...?

355
00:17:46,797 --> 00:17:49,391
这是个自由国度 他总可以辞职
It's a free country. He can always resign.

356
00:17:49,597 --> 00:17:50,766
怎能这么对首相?
How can you treat the PM like this?

357
00:17:50,767 --> 00:17:52,398
他当然担心圣乔治岛
Surely he is right to worry about St George's IS.

358
00:17:52,499 --> 00:17:54,188
毕竟那是个民主国家
After all, It is the democracy!

359
00:17:54,477 --> 00:17:55,217
很快就不是了
Not for long.

360
00:17:56,006 --> 00:17:57,538
这是最新的电报
This is the fresh telegram.

361
00:17:57,539 --> 00:17:59,464
东也门正筹备入侵
The East Yemen are preparing to invade

362
00:17:59,465 --> 00:18:01,313
以支援左翼游击队
in support of the Marxist guerrillas.

363
00:18:01,410 --> 00:18:03,009
真糟糕      是也不是
That's awful.        Yes and no.

364
00:18:03,050 --> 00:18:06,751
对圣乔治政府糟透了
It is moderately bad news for the government of St George's,

365
00:18:06,752 --> 00:18:08,796
但对游击队很好
but very good for the guerrillas.

366
00:18:09,397 --> 00:18:10,927
那岛民怎么办?
What about the islanders?

367
00:18:10,928 --> 00:18:13,217
伯纳 你说话像个政客
Bernard, you're reacting like a politician.

368
00:18:14,597 --> 00:18:16,986
对不起 但我们怎么帮他们?      什么都不做
What are we going to do to help them?        Nothing.

369
00:18:16,988 --> 00:18:18,796
要是他们请求我们呢?
What if St George's appeals to us?

370
00:18:18,831 --> 00:18:21,824
我们给他们一切支持 除了帮忙
We'll give them every support, short of help.

371
00:18:22,774 --> 00:18:24,861
要是首相非要帮助?
What if the Prime Minister insists that we help them?

372
00:18:24,862 --> 00:18:27,831
那就遵从"四阶战术"
Then we follow the four-stage strategy.

373
00:18:28,157 --> 00:18:28,690
是什么?
What's that?

374
00:18:28,691 --> 00:18:32,417
外交部标准危机应对策略
The standard F.O. response in a time of crisis.

375
00:18:32,917 --> 00:18:35,909
第一阶段 我们宣称什么事都没有
In stage one we say nothing is going to happen.

376
00:18:36,117 --> 00:18:39,427
第二阶段 说也许有事发生 但我们不该采取行动
Stage two, it may happen, but we should do nothing.

377
00:18:39,637 --> 00:18:41,836
第三阶段 说也许应该行动
Stage three, maybe we should do something about it,

378
00:18:41,837 --> 00:18:43,518
但我们什么都做不了
but there's nothing we can do.

379
00:18:44,315 --> 00:18:46,194
第四阶段 说也许当初能做点什么
Stage four, maybe there was something we could have done,

380
00:18:46,195 --> 00:18:47,298
但现在已太迟了
but it's too late now.

381
00:18:55,957 --> 00:18:58,087
下午的电报 首相
Afternoon telegrams, Prime Minister.

382
00:18:59,837 --> 00:19:00,488
谢谢 路克
Thank you, Luke.

383
00:19:03,357 --> 00:19:06,845
伯纳在哪?       他在汉弗莱爵士那
Where's Bernard?        I think he's with Sir Humphrey.

384
00:19:08,117 --> 00:19:11,996
东也门有部队调动?       并不严重
Troop movements in East Yemen?        It's not significant.

385
00:19:12,197 --> 00:19:15,075
美国大使提过东也门
The American ambassador mentioned it.

386
00:19:15,277 --> 00:19:17,871
真的? 他竟然还听说过
Really? I'm surprised he'd heard of it.

387
00:19:18,037 --> 00:19:19,280
他们要做什么?
What are they up to?

388
00:19:19,281 --> 00:19:22,495
只是准备对西也门进行常规侵略
Just preparing a regular raid on West Yemen.

389
00:19:22,757 --> 00:19:24,081
我们没什么好担心的?
Nothing for us to worry about?

390
00:19:24,082 --> 00:19:25,610
完全不必担心 首相
Nothing at all.  Prime Minister

391
00:19:25,957 --> 00:19:29,347
他还提到了圣乔治岛
He said something about St George's, too.

392
00:19:29,557 --> 00:19:32,230
真的? 真有学问
Really? Educated man.

393
00:19:33,757 --> 00:19:36,032
作为美国人
For an American.

394
00:19:36,237 --> 00:19:37,315
那边有问题吗?
Is there a problem there?

395
00:19:37,316 --> 00:19:41,231
不不 首相 常规内部争议
No, no, no. Prime Minister,Just the normal local squabbles.

396
00:19:41,477 --> 00:19:44,398
他担心共产党会接管
He seems worried about a Communist take it over.

397
00:19:44,399 --> 00:19:45,973
美国人总是担心
Americans always are.

398
00:19:46,637 --> 00:19:49,231
路克 你看过这个吗?
Luke! Have you read this?

399
00:19:49,397 --> 00:19:52,287
我们昨晚在联合国投票反对以色列
We voted against Israel in the U.N. last night!

400
00:19:52,288 --> 00:19:53,573
看过 首相
Yes, Prime Minister.

401
00:19:53,877 --> 00:19:56,588
但我明确指示要弃权的
But I gave express instructions to abstain.

402
00:19:56,589 --> 00:19:58,204
不会吧 首相
I think not. Prime Minister

403
00:19:58,637 --> 00:20:02,596
我明明告诉外交部长 我强烈认为我们不该偏袒
I said I felt very strongly that we should not take sides.

404
00:20:02,797 --> 00:20:05,526
外交部长知道您的强烈看法
The Foreign Secretary noted your feeling.

405
00:20:05,527 --> 00:20:06,875
但没照办
But did nothing about it!

406
00:20:07,357 --> 00:20:08,687
恕我直言 首相 他办了
With respect, Prime Minister, he did.

407
00:20:08,688 --> 00:20:12,388
他问了我们的联合国大使是否该考虑弃权
He asked our U.N. ambassador if we should consider abstaining.

408
00:20:12,437 --> 00:20:14,428
大使怎么答复?      他说不行
What did he do?        He said no.

409
00:20:15,552 --> 00:20:17,120
你是说外交部可以
You mean the Foreign Office can simply

410
00:20:17,121 --> 00:20:18,708
忽略首相的意愿?
ignore the Prime Minister?

411
00:20:19,197 --> 00:20:20,891
当然不 首相 不
Certainly not, Prime Minister. No.

412
00:20:20,892 --> 00:20:23,642
他们作决定时会充分考虑您的意见
They take full account of you when coming to their decision,

413
00:20:24,357 --> 00:20:25,435
但事情发展太快
but events move rapidly.

414
00:20:25,436 --> 00:20:28,961
我们与阿拉伯关系中有些重要因素
There were important factors in our relationship with the Arabs

415
00:20:29,317 --> 00:20:31,617
您昨晚考虑时并不知情
that were not known to you when you took your view.

416
00:20:31,618 --> 00:20:34,357
我们没法及时通知您
We couldn't get through to you in time.

417
00:20:34,477 --> 00:20:37,275
我有电话的
I am on the phone, you know.

418
00:20:37,437 --> 00:20:40,907
我们觉得没有重要到值得在凌晨3点打扰您
It wasn't sufficiently important to wake you at 3 am.

419
00:20:41,117 --> 00:20:44,029
非常重要 白宫会大发雷霆的
It was extremely important! The White House will do its nut!

420
00:20:44,237 --> 00:20:46,874
本来可以每次联合国投票前都打电话通知您
You could be telephoned before every U.N. vote,

421
00:20:46,875 --> 00:20:49,333
但他们开会时每晚投票两三次
but there are two or three a night.

422
00:20:49,757 --> 00:20:50,451
我怎样才能扭转局势?
What can I do to reverse this?

423
00:20:50,452 --> 00:20:53,000
什么都不做 首相 不然就尴尬了
Nothing. That would be most embarrassing.

424
00:20:54,517 --> 00:20:56,985
政府政策一经陈述 便不容撤消
Once stated, policy can't be retracted.

425
00:20:57,997 --> 00:21:00,957
路克 我要与以色列大使谈谈
I'd like to talk to the Israeli ambassador.

426
00:21:00,958 --> 00:21:03,045
不要 首相
I think not, Prime Minister.

427
00:21:04,237 --> 00:21:07,035
我要与以色列大使谈谈
I want to talk to the Israeli ambassador.

428
00:21:07,237 --> 00:21:09,751
恕我直言 首相 这太不明智了
If I may say so, it would be rather unwise.

429
00:21:09,957 --> 00:21:11,839
路克 能听见我说话吗? 看着我的嘴
Luke! Can you hear me? Watch my lips!

430
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:14,840
我想与以色列大使谈谈
I want to talk to the Israeli ambassador!

431
00:21:16,357 --> 00:21:18,746
当然 首相 如果您一定要的话
Of course, Prime Minister, if that is your wish.

432
00:21:18,917 --> 00:21:20,341
我会联系外交部长和理查爵士
I will contact the Foreign Secretary and Sir Richard

433
00:21:20,342 --> 00:21:22,623
然后打电话给以色列...
and then telephone the Israeli...

434
00:21:22,664 --> 00:21:24,384
我不想找外交部长和理查爵士
I don't want the Foreign Secretary and Sir Richard!

435
00:21:24,385 --> 00:21:25,703
我只想见大使
I just want the ambassador

436
00:21:25,748 --> 00:21:29,990
首相 绕开外交部长
Prime Minister, it would be most improper to see

437
00:21:29,991 --> 00:21:31,614
单独见他太不合适了
him without the Foreign Secretary present.

438
00:21:31,626 --> 00:21:34,174
为什么? 你以为我要谈什么?
Why? What do you think I want to talk to the ambassador about?

439
00:21:34,175 --> 00:21:36,133
大概是联合国的投票
Presumably the vote at the U.N.

440
00:21:36,477 --> 00:21:39,499
是吗? 那就不合适了      哦
Really? That would be most improper.        Oh.

441
00:21:39,599 --> 00:21:41,162
我女儿露茜想找个
My daughter Lucy wishes to spend her

442
00:21:41,163 --> 00:21:42,629
以色列集体农场渡假
next long vacation on a kibbutz.

443
00:21:43,008 --> 00:21:45,999
或者说 除了苏塞克斯大学
Or I should say, as she's at the University of Sussex,

444
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:47,076
另一个集体农场
another kibbutz.

445
00:21:49,477 --> 00:21:53,072
知道了      我们在伦敦政经学院是同学
I see.        The ambassador and I were at the LSE.

446
00:21:53,237 --> 00:21:55,114
我想邀他今晚来我家喝酒
I thought I'd invite him to the flat tonight for a drink.

447
00:21:55,115 --> 00:21:58,248
大约6点 请你安排一下 路克?
6 pm will be convenient. See to it, would you, Luke?

448
00:21:59,682 --> 00:22:02,118
好的 首相      谢谢
Yes, Prime Minister.        Thank you.

449
00:22:08,877 --> 00:22:12,337
别生气 吉姆 这经常发生
Don't be upset, Jim. It happens all the time.

450
00:22:12,338 --> 00:22:14,089
我说了要弃权
I told them to abstain.

451
00:22:14,517 --> 00:22:16,954
众所周知 在英国外交部
It's well known that in the British Foreign Office

452
00:22:16,955 --> 00:22:18,619
首相发的指示
an instruction from the Prime Minister

453
00:22:18,719 --> 00:22:21,026
会被外交部长转成请求
becomes a request from the Foreign Secretary,

454
00:22:21,027 --> 00:22:23,620
国务大臣转成推荐
a recommendation from the Minister of State

455
00:22:23,720 --> 00:22:26,852
到大使那就成了建议
and, finally, a suggestion to the ambassador.

456
00:22:26,853 --> 00:22:28,539
如果它能走那么远
If it ever gets that far.

457
00:22:28,757 --> 00:22:31,146
谢谢 干杯
Thank you. L'Chaim.

458
00:22:31,317 --> 00:22:33,114
干杯
Cheers.

459
00:22:33,277 --> 00:22:37,095
吉姆 你要怎么处理圣乔治岛的事?
Well, Jim, what are you going to do about St George's?

460
00:22:37,437 --> 00:22:40,634
你也知道?      当然
You know about that?        Obviously.

461
00:22:40,797 --> 00:22:42,512
没什么大问题吧, 是吗?
Not a serious problem, is it?

462
00:22:42,513 --> 00:22:45,200
你的情报自然比我的好
it isn`t,yes.Your information must be better than mine.

463
00:22:45,597 --> 00:22:47,015
我的来自外交部
Mine comes from the Foreign Office.

464
00:22:49,357 --> 00:22:51,274
以色列情报处说
Israeli Intelligence says

465
00:22:51,374 --> 00:22:53,525
东也门最近几天会
that East Yemen are going to invade

466
00:22:53,526 --> 00:22:56,017
入侵圣乔治岛
St George's Island in the next few days.

467
00:22:56,117 --> 00:22:56,829
什么?
What?!

468
00:22:58,077 --> 00:22:59,803
原来是这样
So that's the connection.

469
00:22:59,804 --> 00:23:02,956
你的外交部与东也门达成协议
Your Foreign Office agreed with East Yemen

470
00:23:03,037 --> 00:23:05,964
他们会表面采取强硬外交手段
that they'll make strong diplomatic representations,

471
00:23:05,965 --> 00:23:07,075
但实际什么也不做
but do nothing.

472
00:23:07,511 --> 00:23:11,161
回报是 东也门接管圣乔治岛后维持机场合约
In return, you keep your airport contract.

473
00:23:11,261 --> 00:23:12,418
会有骚乱的
There will be uproar!

474
00:23:12,717 --> 00:23:13,756
但那只是开始
That's only the start.

475
00:23:13,856 --> 00:23:16,548
驻华盛顿大使恰好告诉我
I happen to know from our ambassador in Washington

476
00:23:16,549 --> 00:23:17,873
美国将会支援
the Americans are going to support

477
00:23:17,874 --> 00:23:18,874
圣乔治现任政府
the present government of St George's .

478
00:23:19,625 --> 00:23:23,713
在联合国...?      不 在战争中 在岛上
In the U.N...?        No, in battle. On St George's Island.

479
00:23:23,947 --> 00:23:25,922
他们将派遣一个空降师进岛
They are sending an airborne division

480
00:23:25,923 --> 00:23:27,564
第七舰队做后援
backed up by the Seventh Fleet.

481
00:23:27,641 --> 00:23:30,073
美国侵略一个英联邦国家?
The American is invading a Commonwealth country?

482
00:23:31,055 --> 00:23:34,590
皇室会勃然大怒 我会出足洋相
The Palace will hit the roof. And I'll look ridiculous.

483
00:23:34,757 --> 00:23:37,555
美国为何不告诉我?      他们不信任你
Why didn't they tell me?        They don't trust you.

484
00:23:37,556 --> 00:23:37,887
为什么？
Why not？

485
00:23:38,237 --> 00:23:40,338
因为你相信外交部
Because you trust the Foreign Office.

486
00:23:40,339 --> 00:23:43,533
哦, 是这样. 我能怎么做?
Oh, I see. What can I do about it?

487
00:23:43,917 --> 00:23:48,513
吉姆 你在德国有支空降军队待命
Jim, you have an airborne battalion on standby in Germany

488
00:23:48,677 --> 00:23:51,066
现在不需参加北约演习
that is not now needed for the NATO exercise.

489
00:23:51,277 --> 00:23:54,269
你怎么知道?      我就是知道
How do you know?        I know.

490
00:23:54,957 --> 00:23:58,161
如果你把他们派到圣乔治岛
Now, if you were to send it to St George's Island,

491
00:23:58,162 --> 00:24:00,147
必能吓退东也门
it would frighten off East Yemen.

492
00:24:00,397 --> 00:24:02,560
他们绝不敢入侵
They'd never dare invade.

493
00:24:02,660 --> 00:24:05,371
当然 不该由以色列大使
Of course, it's not for the Israeli ambassador

494
00:24:05,372 --> 00:24:07,330
给英国首相提建议
to advise the British Prime Minister.

495
00:24:08,078 --> 00:24:09,858
首相也不会采纳你的建议
And he wouldn't take your advice anyway.

496
00:24:13,357 --> 00:24:16,574
找外交部长和国防部长
Get me the Foreign Secretary and the Defence Secretary.

497
00:24:17,870 --> 00:24:19,946
我在想外交部为何没有掩护自己
I wonder why the Foreign Office didn't cover themselves.

498
00:24:21,228 --> 00:24:22,527
也许他们有
Maybe they did.

499
00:24:22,877 --> 00:24:24,618
今晚他们给了我几箱文件
They gave me several boxes tonight.

500
00:24:24,619 --> 00:24:26,753
除了这个我都看了
I've been through them all except this one.

501
00:24:28,991 --> 00:24:30,224
我想会不会就是这个
I wonder if this could be it.

502
00:24:30,597 --> 00:24:33,744
"北印度洋形势报告"
''Northern Indian Ocean Situation Report''.

503
00:24:34,597 --> 00:24:36,986
有138页 就是它了
It's 138 pages. It must be it.

504
00:24:40,076 --> 00:24:41,674
喂? 是的 罗尼
Hello? Yes, Ronnie.

505
00:24:42,277 --> 00:24:44,781
我要圣乔治岛总统
I want the president of St George's Island to

506
00:24:44,782 --> 00:24:47,328
邀请一支英国空降军队
invite Britain to send an airborne battalion

507
00:24:47,363 --> 00:24:49,826
进行善意访问
on a goodwill visit.

508
00:24:49,997 --> 00:24:52,386
不 只是表示友好 善意的
No, just a friendly gesture. Goodwill.

509
00:24:52,557 --> 00:24:55,788
好 请马上办 谢谢
Yes, at once, please. Thank you.

510
00:24:56,578 --> 00:24:59,017
他好像认为一次善意访问
He seemed to think that 800 fully-armed paratroopers

511
00:24:59,018 --> 00:25:01,821
派800名全副武装的伞兵太多了
was an awful lot to send on a goodwill visit.

512
00:25:04,197 --> 00:25:06,989
不 我们善意太多了
No, it's just an awful lot of goodwill.

513
00:25:09,518 --> 00:25:13,245
对 保罗 你有支空降军队
Oh, yes, Paul. You know you have an airborne battalion

514
00:25:13,546 --> 00:25:14,764
在德国待命?
on standby in Germany?

515
00:25:15,630 --> 00:25:17,280
我怎么知道的不重要
Never mind how I know.

516
00:25:17,557 --> 00:25:19,185
既然现在没任务
Well, since it's not being used,

517
00:25:19,186 --> 00:25:21,822
我想让他们马上飞到圣乔治岛
I want them to fly straight off to St George's Island.

518
00:25:23,232 --> 00:25:25,521
大概在非洲和印度之间
Sort of between Africa and India.

519
00:25:27,157 --> 00:25:29,805
善意访问 只打一下旗帜
A goodwill visit. Just showing the flag.

520
00:25:30,837 --> 00:25:35,568
邀请已经发出了 对 6小时后出发
They have been invited. Yes. Leave in...six hours.

521
00:25:36,437 --> 00:25:39,123
对 临时善意访问
Yes, an instant goodwill visit.

522
00:25:39,223 --> 00:25:41,097
让宣传办马上发布消息
Tell your press office to announce it at once.

523
00:25:41,757 --> 00:25:44,889
不不 不要提到我 只是常规访问
No, no, leave me out of it. A routine visit.

524
00:25:45,417 --> 00:25:48,002
好吧 一次常规的惊喜访问
All right. A routine surprise visit.

525
00:25:49,157 --> 00:25:50,975
就说他们早就得到邀请
Well, say they were invited earlier,

526
00:25:50,976 --> 00:25:52,932
只是北约演习耽误了行程
but the NATO exercise got in the way.

527
00:25:53,717 --> 00:25:55,141
现在完事了 他们就来了
Now they're not needed, they're going.

528
00:25:56,242 --> 00:25:58,673
没关系 没人知道是假的
All right. Nobody knows it's not true.

529
00:25:58,877 --> 00:26:01,471
媒体发消息又不用宣誓
Press statements aren't delivered under oath.

530
00:26:03,357 --> 00:26:05,721
他们午夜就出发
They'll be off at midnight.

531
00:26:06,164 --> 00:26:08,590
我听说空中有支空降军队
I gather that there's an airborne battalion in the air.

532
00:26:09,214 --> 00:26:10,498
那不是正好嘛
Sounds like the right place for it

533
00:26:13,757 --> 00:26:16,067
我听说它正飞向圣乔治岛
I gather it's on its way to St George's.

534
00:26:16,068 --> 00:26:18,642
对 2小时内就该到了
Yes, it should land in two hours time.

535
00:26:19,437 --> 00:26:21,096
会不会太突然了?
Isn't this all rather sudden?

536
00:26:21,403 --> 00:26:23,779
我突然有表示友好的冲动 汉弗莱
I had a sudden friendly impulse. Humphrey

537
00:26:24,197 --> 00:26:25,558
我想传播一点善意
I wanted to spread a little goodwill.

538
00:26:26,045 --> 00:26:28,834
今早外交部可没多少善意
There's not much goodwill in the F.O. this morning

539
00:26:29,157 --> 00:26:30,437
真的 为什么?
Really? Why not?

540
00:26:30,438 --> 00:26:32,660
这可以理解为挑衅
It might be construed as provocative,

541
00:26:32,702 --> 00:26:35,120
派遣一支全副武装的空降军队
sending a fully-armed airborne battalion

542
00:26:35,220 --> 00:26:38,535
进入一个爆炸性地区
into a trouble spot like that, an explosive situation.

543
00:26:38,635 --> 00:26:40,999
爆炸性? 你不是说没问题嘛
Explosive? I thought there was no problem there.

544
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:43,283
是没有 真的
Eh...well, yes, indeed.

545
00:26:43,717 --> 00:26:47,560
没问题 但有潜在的爆炸性
There is no problem, but it's explosive potentially.

546
00:26:47,757 --> 00:26:52,106
为什么?      调遣军队总有潜在爆炸性
Why?        Moving troops is always potentially explosive.

547
00:26:52,557 --> 00:26:54,868
在索尔兹伯里平原(英格兰)调来调去
We move them around Salisbury Plain.

548
00:26:54,869 --> 00:26:56,782
也有潜在爆炸性?
Is that potentially explosive?

549
00:26:57,157 --> 00:27:00,186
有很多未爆弹在...
There are a lot of unexploded shells on...

550
00:27:01,077 --> 00:27:02,279
谢谢 伯纳
Thank you, Bernard.

551
00:27:02,280 --> 00:27:05,082
请告诉我外交部担心什么
Do tell me why the Foreign Office is worried.

552
00:27:05,117 --> 00:27:06,331
我很感兴趣
I'm fascinated.

553
00:27:06,717 --> 00:27:09,379
这是个敏感地区 不稳定
It's a sensitive part of the world. Unstable.

554
00:27:09,380 --> 00:27:11,190
他们总告诉我非常稳定
They always tell me how stable it is.

555
00:27:11,557 --> 00:27:14,435
对 它确实...很稳定
Well, yes, indeed it is...very,

556
00:27:14,597 --> 00:27:18,431
但那是种...不稳定的稳定
but it's a sort of...unstable sort of stability.

557
00:27:19,917 --> 00:27:22,576
打扰了 汉弗莱爵士      什么事 路克?
Excuse me, Sir Humphrey.        Yes, Luke.

558
00:27:22,877 --> 00:27:24,719
外交部的电报 首相
Foreign Office telegrams. Prime Minister.

559
00:27:24,720 --> 00:27:27,860
谢谢 路克 天 还真多
Thank you, Luke. Oh, gosh. Rather a lot.

560
00:27:28,037 --> 00:27:30,517
是的 对圣乔治岛的
Yes, the somewhat unorthodox visit

561
00:27:30,518 --> 00:27:32,371
非正统访问有结果了
to St George's has stirred things up.

562
00:27:33,077 --> 00:27:36,868
啊 东也门把部队调回基地了
Ah, I see East Yemen is moving its troops back to base.

563
00:27:37,277 --> 00:27:38,265
是的 首相
Yes, Prime Minister.

564
00:27:38,266 --> 00:27:41,415
又不想入侵西也门了?
Decided not to invade West Yemen after all?

565
00:27:41,877 --> 00:27:44,599
好像是      太好了
So it seems.        Oh, this is nice.

566
00:27:44,699 --> 00:27:48,704
美国对我们的小访问感到高兴 不错嘛
The Americans are delighted by our visit. That's good.

567
00:27:48,797 --> 00:27:51,033
非常好 首相
Excellent, Prime Minister.

568
00:27:51,408 --> 00:27:53,797
他们说若需要巩固 
They say they are going to hold airborne division ready

569
00:27:53,798 --> 00:27:54,874
他们有一整个空降师待命
 if we want reinforcements.

570
00:27:54,909 --> 00:27:56,285
巩固什么?
Reinforcements of what?

571
00:27:57,139 --> 00:27:59,872
巩固善意 汉弗莱
Reinforcements of goodwill, Humphrey.

572
00:28:01,597 --> 00:28:06,432
首相 请问您为何要搞这种恶作剧?
May I inquire where the impulse for this little escapade came from?

573
00:28:06,637 --> 00:28:09,907
当然可以 路克提议的      路克?
Of course you may. It came from Luke.        Luke?!

574
00:28:10,597 --> 00:28:12,553
我?
From me?

575
00:28:12,757 --> 00:28:13,865
是你起草了那份
It was you who put together that

576
00:28:13,866 --> 00:28:17,175
精彩的"北印度洋形势报告" 对吗?
masterly Northern Indian Ocean Situation Report, wasn`t it?

577
00:28:17,784 --> 00:28:20,014
对 可论点是什么都不用做
Yes, but it argued for not doing anything.

578
00:28:20,422 --> 00:28:23,122
得啦 路克 你骗不了我      什么?
Come off it, Luke. You can't fool me.        What?!

579
00:28:23,637 --> 00:28:25,771
我能体会言外之意
I can read between the lines.

580
00:28:26,818 --> 00:28:30,310
有些政治家对外交有直觉
Some politicians have a feeling for foreign affairs.

581
00:28:30,477 --> 00:28:33,913
我知道你是说圣乔治岛需要支援
I knew you meant St George's needed support.

582
00:28:34,117 --> 00:28:36,711
对 呃 其实不是的
Oh, yes. Well, no, actually.

583
00:28:37,717 --> 00:28:40,356
只在107页有一段
Only in one paragraph on page 107.

584
00:28:40,557 --> 00:28:42,946
足够了 我明白这个暗示
It was enough. I can take the hint.

585
00:28:43,117 --> 00:28:44,363
我全归功于你
I'm giving you full credit for it.

586
00:28:44,364 --> 00:28:48,194
我告诉外交部长是你提醒的
I told the Foreign Secretary it was your warning sparked it off.

587
00:28:48,294 --> 00:28:52,341
不不 不是的 您不会吧?
No, no, it wasn't You haven't?

588
00:28:52,441 --> 00:28:55,703
你当然也猜到了
And I don't think I'm giving away any secrets

589
00:28:55,704 --> 00:28:57,731
一定会报答你的
when I say you are going to be rewarded.

590
00:28:57,831 --> 00:29:03,291
报答?      任命你为一个重要使馆的大使
Rewarded?        Ambassador at a very important embassy.

591
00:29:03,576 --> 00:29:05,701
哪个使馆?      特拉维夫
Which embassy?        Tel Aviv.

592
00:29:05,723 --> 00:29:09,556
天哪 您不能派我去以色列
Oh, my God! You can't send me to Israel.

593
00:29:09,557 --> 00:29:10,740
想想我的前途
Think about my career.

594
00:29:10,793 --> 00:29:13,655
别傻了 这是荣誉 是晋升
Don't be absurd. It's an honour. Promotion.

595
00:29:13,752 --> 00:29:15,163
但以色列人会不高兴的
Yse, it will upset Israelis.

596
00:29:15,164 --> 00:29:15,753
他们不喜欢我
They won't want me.

597
00:29:15,754 --> 00:29:17,406
他们知道我是阿拉伯那边的
They know I'm on the Arab side.

598
00:29:18,787 --> 00:29:20,302
我以为你是我们这边的
I thought you were on our side.

599
00:29:20,303 --> 00:29:21,469
当然 可是...
Of course, yes, but...

600
00:29:21,920 --> 00:29:24,655
我们需要你这样的人去特拉维夫
We need somebody like you in Tel Aviv

601
00:29:24,690 --> 00:29:27,711
解释我们为何在联合国投票反对他们
to explain why we always vote against them in the UN.

602
00:29:28,790 --> 00:29:30,010
不是么? 汉弗莱?
Don't we, Humphrey?

603
00:29:31,277 --> 00:29:33,101
是 首相
Yes, Prime Minister.

604
00:29:35,505 --> 00:29:45,570
<font color="#4096d1">破烂熊字幕组 -==www.RagBear.com==-
